<title>GERMANY: CLT-UFA lost 250 mln DM on Club RTL - Bertelsmann.</title>
<headline>CLT-UFA lost 250 mln DM on Club RTL - Bertelsmann.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soon-to-be-merged satellite TV firms CLT and UFA lost around 250 million marks ($160 million) through their involvement in the failed Club RTL digital venture, a source at UFA's owner Bertelsmann AG said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CLT, owned by Groupe Bruxelles Lambert and Havas of France, will merge with Bertelsmann's UFA from the start of 1997. The Club RTL loss will hit profits in CLT-UFA's first year, the source confirmed.</p>
<p>The source's comments partially confirmed a report from the Spiegel news weekly released ahead of publication, which quoted the venture's budget saying that 1997 profits would be between 50 and 100 million marks on turnover of five billion marks.</p>
<p>But, Spiegel added, profits should increase after 1997, with a target of 600 million marks in 2001 on turnover of six billion marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.559 German Marks)</p>
